{"id": "EUVD-2026-80297", "enisaUuid": "44491bea-5958-35d2-838f-ab705ed6e03c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: vnifilter: enforce exact length of GROUP/GROUP6 attributes\n\nThe VXLAN VNI filter entry policy declares the GROUP/GROUP6 address\nattributes as NLA_BINARY with only a maximum length, so validate_nla()\naccepts a payload shorter than the address. The GROUP consumer reads it\nwith nla_get_in_addr(), an unconditional 4-byte load, so a short\nattribute over-reads up to 3 bytes of uninitialised slab data, which are\nstored into remote_ip and echoed back via RTM_GETTUNNEL, disclosing\nkernel memory.\n\nSwitch both entries to NLA_POLICY_EXACT_LEN() so the validator rejects\nany GROUP/GROUP6 that is not exactly 4 / 16 bytes; a valid address is\nalways sent at full width.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T08:48:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e12c4663529699f457b2988c1dfedf4d13b3b3be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47bfcc871576eaef6c8edab6749acd4b317306ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9ec10815199f9879ba080241dc555efb1daf324", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/daebc7064a1b4c12c98e52c4bceede7f2fcd573c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad32e564c62ebf5ba76dd60a22af52c69d54d17b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/984f831dda31b3a18f47454cf64989f65402879e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89776", "GHSA-vf8c-65h3-589v"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06ced928-edd2-3d7c-bb6e-789dc76d90a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9c4bb0b245cee35ef66f75bf409c9573d934cf9 <47bfcc871576eaef6c8edab6749acd4b317306ea"}, {"id": "090c4965-3fdc-37c2-aca1-706783dbec49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "16a51120-f91a-3c35-8065-b3ab5830ebb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9c4bb0b245cee35ef66f75bf409c9573d934cf9 <ad32e564c62ebf5ba76dd60a22af52c69d54d17b"}, {"id": "25bc7d5d-050f-3ae2-8362-e4849e12f26e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "33330aa7-4391-3344-a84f-acadf3d0e7d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.18"}, {"id": "34787d3a-f00a-3757-a28b-263dc6f6671c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9c4bb0b245cee35ef66f75bf409c9573d934cf9 <a9ec10815199f9879ba080241dc555efb1daf324"}, {"id": "356099c0-eeb5-3947-9c0b-78ebc2d084b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9c4bb0b245cee35ef66f75bf409c9573d934cf9 <e12c4663529699f457b2988c1dfedf4d13b3b3be"}, {"id": "555ac04d-b9e9-31ff-afbf-5991d8ac17c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9c4bb0b245cee35ef66f75bf409c9573d934cf9 <daebc7064a1b4c12c98e52c4bceede7f2fcd573c"}, {"id": "5bbf6db1-88fd-3c57-91b3-e025dd641a72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "7000438f-1248-3fde-9e2d-c6e685c22003", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "bb7bb44b-68e8-3eeb-a753-07ecdf3cab81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9c4bb0b245cee35ef66f75bf409c9573d934cf9 <984f831dda31b3a18f47454cf64989f65402879e"}, {"id": "c9595607-ff62-38dc-84aa-8f32191c23af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cc02021c-b27b-3bee-bb6b-9319723821b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ff75bd9d-9537-3887-9332-0744f5e81a4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ace461e3-48fe-36c3-8b65-6e8230710876", "vendor